@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: how the workspace is scanned for projects, and what bounds the walk
' covers: internal/workspace/scan*.go
'   the symlink walk that reuses the deny set .. _spec/internal/workspace/mount-symlink-escape.puml
'   the dind gate this scan once fed ........... _spec/_paradigms/retire-dind.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── THE SCAN LIVES IN WORKSPACE (DECIDED 2026-11-15) ───────────────────────
' DECIDED 2026-11-15 (owner: "the 8 uncontested"; codebase-compression.puml
' P11, F3 option 1): the scan, a leaf package imported by workspace and
' posture, is internal/workspace's scan.go, and this file moved with it.
' posture now imports workspace (L4 → L1, no edge points up). Renamed:
' ScanResult, ScanMaxDepth, DefaultScanBudget; the test helper that
' duplicated mount_test.go's touch is gone.
title Workspace scan — one walker, monorepo-aware, dependency trees pruned

node "internal/workspace scan.go" as PKG <<host>> {
  component "Scan(scopeDir, repoRoot,\nmarkers, budget) ScanResult" as SCAN <<app>>
  component "alwaysPrune\nhardcoded deny set" as HARD <<app>>
  component "gitignoreNames(dir)\nplain basenames only" as GI <<app>>
}

folder "Consumers" as USE <<host>> {
  component "choice prompt header\ntooling row" as HDR <<app>>
}

database "workspace tree\ndepth <= ScanMaxDepth (7)" as TREE <<db>>
component "unpruned dependency tree\n→ a dependency's files read as the project's" as BAD <<error>>

SCAN ARROW_MAIN HARD : always applied
SCAN ARROW_OPTIONAL GI : scope AND repo root, additive
SCAN ARROW_MAIN TREE : walk, budgeted
HDR ARROW_MAIN SCAN
GI ARROW_ERROR BAD : gitignore alone is not enough

note right of GI
  **.gitignore alone was unsafe.** Lookup
  stopped at the first ""\.gitignore"" walking
  up, so a monorepo scope with its own file
  never saw the repo root's ""node_modules"".
end note

note right of GI
  **The bug this replaced.** A scope of
  ""apps/web"" whose ""\.gitignore"" listed only
  ""\.next/"" walked straight into
  ""apps/web/node_modules"" to depth 7.
end note

note left of GI
  **Two more holes.** A pattern holding / * ? [
  cannot prune a basename, so
  ""**/node_modules"" never matched, and a repo
  on ""core.excludesFile"" supplied nothing.
end note

note bottom of GI
  **So the derived names are additive only.**
  They come from the scope //and// the repo
  root, on top of a set that always applies.
end note

note bottom of BAD
  **Wrong, not merely wasteful.** npm packages
  ship Dockerfiles, so a repo with none of its
  own was once offered a ""--privileged""
  sidecar through ""dind.ScopeHasDockerfiles"".
end note

note right of BAD
  **The deny set stays hardcoded.** That gate
  left with the sidecar and the walker only
  labels a prompt now, but a scan that reports
  a dependency's files as the project's is
  wrong whatever reads it.
end note

note bottom of TREE
  **Bounded three ways.** Depth stops at
  ""ScanMaxDepth"" (7, as in the walker this
  replaced), and ""DefaultScanBudget"" caps the
  entries examined.
end note

note right of TREE
  **A pathological tree must degrade.** The
  scan runs before the container exists, in
  front of an operator at a prompt, so it may
  not stall.
end note

note left of TREE
  **The walk stops early.** It exits once every
  marker is found, which is shallow in practice:
  files at each level are read before descending.
end note

note top of TREE
  **Truncation is logged, never shown.** A
  bounded scan sets ""ScanResult.Truncated"";
  the prompt header stays about the workspace,
  and the run log tells whoever needs to know.
end note

note left of HARD
  **One deny set, three walks.** This scan, the
  mount planner's symlink walk and the
  in-container ""_proveo_walk"" ask one question,
  so ""AlwaysPrune"" is exported: three private
  copies drift the moment one is corrected.
end note

note bottom of HARD
  **Package stores earn their place.**
  ""\.pnpm-store"" held 110k of the 123k files
  the in-container walk crossed on one monorepo,
  and a content-addressed store object with no
  extension is never workspace source.
end note

note top of HARD
  **The store names arrived late.** This scan's
  budget usually stops before it reaches a
  store, which is why.
end note

note right of SCAN
  **Markers, not globs.** ""Names"" match a
  basename exactly and ""Suffixes"" match its
  end (""\.go""); either satisfies the marker.
end note

note bottom of SCAN
  **Labels are facts.** Tooling labels are
  reported as found; the ""lsp:"" prediction
  row left with the LSP removal (2026-10-30).
end note
@enduml
